{"type":"result","subtype":"success","is_error":false,"duration_ms":183998,"duration_api_ms":180370,"num_turns":22,"result":"","stop_reason":"end_turn","session_id":"4ebf9af0-93a4-4d2a-9d46-557cfca3164e","total_cost_usd":1.0741885,"usage":{"input_tokens":17,"cache_creation_input_tokens":73236,"cache_read_input_tokens":898457,"output_tokens":6686,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":73236,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"","iterations":[],"speed":"standard"},"modelUsage":{"claude-opus-4-6":{"inputTokens":17,"outputTokens":6686,"cacheReadInputTokens":898457,"cacheCreationInputTokens":73236,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":1.0741885,"contextWindow":200000,"maxOutputTokens":64000}},"permission_denials":[],"structured_output":{"amendments":[{"body":"In `run_probe_biofilter_scaling_bigger_media_faster_cycling_with_suffix`, the `biofilter_filter_area` check error message says \"2× media should expand filter habitat area by >1.5×\" but the actual media configuration is 500 cm² vs 4000 cm² (8× difference, not 2×). Fix the diagnostic string to say \"8× media\" or \"larger media\" so a developer seeing a failure isn't misled about the test setup.","rationale":"Misleading diagnostic output can waste significant debugging time. The error message is the primary artifact a developer sees on failure; having it state '2×' when the setup is 8× creates a false mental model of the scenario configuration."},{"body":"The substrate redox probe (probe 4) intentionally enables aeration for the inert control arm (`state.hardware.aeration.enabled = true; state.hardware.aeration.intensity = 0.6;` at line ~1167) but not the planted arm. The doc comment says it validates 'substrate geometry and root-zone effects' but the aeration asymmetry means it actually validates the combined effect of substrate geometry + DO regime. Add a brief note in the doc comment acknowledging that the two arms differ in aeration, and explain that this strengthens the test: even with higher DO, the thin inert substrate cannot sustain denitrification because it lacks sufficient suboxic volume.","rationale":"A future developer reading just the doc comment ('mature planted substrate shows NO₃ removal that unplanted substrate does not') would expect both arms to share the same aeration regime. The asymmetry is intentional and correct — the planted arm's low-DO, root-zone-driven suboxic zone is part of the ecological story — but un-documented asymmetries in test setups are a common source of confusion during maintenance."}],"summary":"Reviewed the full diff (substrate.rs refactoring, e2e_habitat_geometry_probes.rs 1640-line addition, shrimp parameter additions across presets/scenarios/validation/save_load, and the root_zone_oxygenation test comment update). All 5 probes pass. The substrate.rs refactoring to avoid redundant `compute_habitat_registry` calls is clean and the new `ROOT_RESPIRATION_SUBSTRATE_DEMAND_FRACTION` term is correctly wired. The `_with_registry` internal API pattern is sound. Shrimp parameter additions (`low_temp_repro_ramp_width_c`, `tan_repro_full_suppression_mg_n_per_l`, `no2_repro_full_suppression_mg_n_per_l`) are consistently propagated across all required touch points (toml, presets, scenarios, validation, save_load). The test changed from equality to inequality assertion in `zero_rol_rate_zeroes_root_bonus_but_preserves_root_demand_baseline` is mechanistically correct given the new root demand baseline. No safety issues, no correctness bugs found. Two minor documentation/diagnostic amendments proposed."},"fast_mode_state":"off","uuid":"1c8308d6-3e2b-46e2-b036-3594eadc74c7"}
